Hi Mike,

Surely there must be an interaction to measure? Say T define a landmark at the specific point at the bottom of the chin. On some people this point is ambiguous, so if i digitised the same photo twice its unlikely i would place the point in the same identical place both times. so we have digitising error. if i digitise photos from 2 cameras twice each, perhaps this point is easier to see from one camera than the other, and so there would be less digitising variance when looking at photos taken from one camera compared to the other.

Richie

