Subject: Re: [geomorph-r-package] Procustes aligning faces
Message-ID: <XjzXAJZphq0.xBnxbGW7BgAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <XjzXAJZphq0.FFaaO5g5BAAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
References: <XjzXAJZphq0.FFaaO5g5BAAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/XjzXAJZphq0/m/xBnxbGW7BgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear Richie,

bilat.symmetry is the correct function to use here, and yes, proceed with the $sym.shape 3D array.

You are certainly able to leave those elements out if you wish, it is your study. But the question you have to ask yourself is why you are not averaging your replicates? Performing any analysis after the GPA on all 688 observations will be confounded by pseduoreplication.

Emma

